  {
   "xml_index": 1,
   "xml_name": "L09_001_Create A Dictionary",
   "display_name": "Create A Dictionary",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Welcome to Lab 9! A <b>dictionary</b> stores <b>key: value</b> pairs. Instead of looking up an item by its position (0, 1, 2, ...), as in a list, you look it up by its <b>key</b>, like looking up a word in a real dictionary to find its meaning.</p>\n<p>A dictionary is written with curly braces <code>{ }</code>, with a colon between each key and its value:</p>\n<pre>menu = {&quot;tea&quot;: 10, &quot;coffee&quot;: 25, &quot;samosa&quot;: 15}</pre>\n<table style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:2px 1px;margin:6px 0 4px\"><tr><td rowspan=\"2\" style=\"padding-right:10px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace\">menu =</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:4px 8px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:13px;background:#cfdcec;color:#1f3a63;border-radius:2px 2px 0 0\">&#x27;tea&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:4px 8px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:13px;background:#cfdcec;color:#1f3a63;border-radius:2px 2px 0 0\">&#x27;coffee&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:4px 8px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:13px;background:#cfdcec;color:#1f3a63;border-radius:2px 2px 0 0\">&#x27;samosa&#x27;</td><td style=\"padding-left:8px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">key<br><br>value</td></tr><tr><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 8px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(31,95,153);color:#fff;border-radius:0 0 2px 2px\">10</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 8px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(52,129,188);color:#fff;border-radius:0 0 2px 2px\">25</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 8px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(74,163,223);color:#fff;border-radius:0 0 2px 2px\">15</td></tr></table>\n<pre>menu = {&quot;tea&quot;: 10, &quot;coffee&quot;: 25, &quot;samosa&quot;: 15}\nprint(menu[&quot;coffee&quot;])\nprint(len(menu))\nprint(menu)</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>25\n3\n{&#x27;tea&#x27;: 10, &#x27;coffee&#x27;: 25, &#x27;samosa&#x27;: 15}</pre>\n<p><code>menu[\"coffee\"]</code> gives the value for the key <code>\"coffee\"</code>. <code>len</code> counts the pairs.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the function <code>make_contact(name, phone)</code>, which returns a dictionary with two pairs: the key <code>\"name\"</code> with the value <code>name</code>, and the key <code>\"phone\"</code> with the value <code>phone</code>.</p>\n<p>For example, <code>make_contact(\"Asha\", \"98220\")</code> returns <code>{'name': 'Asha', 'phone': '98220'}</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "def make_contact(name, phone):\n    # write your code here\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your code; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(make_contact(\"Asha\", \"98220\"))\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
