   "xml_name": "L09_006_Safe Access With get",
   "display_name": "Safe Access With get",
   "questiontext_html": "<p><code>d.get(key)</code> is a safe way to read: it returns the value, or <code>None</code> if the key is missing (no error). <code>d.get(key, default)</code> returns <code>default</code> instead of <code>None</code>:</p>\n<pre>stock = {&quot;pens&quot;: 12, &quot;books&quot;: 0}\nprint(stock.get(&quot;pens&quot;))\nprint(stock.get(&quot;bags&quot;))\nprint(stock.get(&quot;bags&quot;, 0))</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>12\nNone\n0</pre>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the function <code>stock_of(stock, item)</code>, which returns how many of <code>item</code> are in the dictionary <code>stock</code>, or <code>0</code> if the item is not listed. Use <code>get</code> with a default.</p>\n<p>For example, <code>stock_of({\"pens\": 12}, \"bags\")</code> returns <code>0</code>.</p>",
