   "xml_name": "L09_007_Checking Many Keys",
   "display_name": "Checking Many Keys",
   "questiontext_html": "<p><code>in</code> checks the keys of a dictionary. To check the <b>values</b>, use <code>x in d.values()</code>:</p>\n<pre>ages = {&quot;Asha&quot;: 19, &quot;Ravi&quot;: 20}\nprint(&quot;Asha&quot; in ages, 19 in ages)\nprint(19 in ages.values())</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>True False\nTrue</pre>\n<p><b>Indentation reminder:</b> the body of an <code>if</code>, loop, function or class must be indented (press Tab or type 4 spaces). Only the spaces at the start of a line matter.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the function <code>has_all(d, keys)</code>, which returns <code>True</code> if <b>every</b> item of the list <code>keys</code> is a key of the dictionary <code>d</code>, and <code>False</code> otherwise. (An empty list of keys gives <code>True</code>.)</p>\n<p>For example, <code>has_all({\"a\": 1, \"b\": 2}, [\"a\", \"b\"])</code> returns <code>True</code>.</p>",
