   "xml_index": 9,
   "xml_name": "L09_009_Add And Update",
   "display_name": "Add And Update",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Dictionaries are <b>mutable</b>. The same assignment <code>d[key] = value</code> either <b>adds</b> a new pair (if the key is new) or <b>updates</b> the value (if the key exists):</p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:2px 1px;margin:6px 0 4px\"><tr><td rowspan=\"2\" style=\"padding-right:10px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace\">menu =</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:4px 8px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:13px;background:#cfdcec;color:#1f3a63;border-radius:2px 2px 0 0\">&#x27;tea&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:4px 8px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:13px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px 2px 0 0\">&#x27;coffee&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:4px 8px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:13px;background:#cfdcec;color:#1f3a63;border-radius:2px 2px 0 0\">&#x27;juice&#x27;</td><td style=\"padding-left:8px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">key<br><br>value</td></tr><tr><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 8px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(31,95,153);color:#fff;border-radius:0 0 2px 2px\">12</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 8px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:0 0 2px 2px\">25</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 8px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(74,163,223);color:#fff;border-radius:0 0 2px 2px\">30</td></tr></table><div style=\"font-size:13px;color:#8a939c;margin:0 0 10px\">menu[&#x27;tea&#x27;] = 12 updated a value; menu[&#x27;juice&#x27;] = 30 added a pair</div>\n<pre>menu = {&quot;tea&quot;: 10, &quot;coffee&quot;: 25}\nmenu[&quot;tea&quot;] = 12\nmenu[&quot;juice&quot;] = 30\nprint(menu)</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>{&#x27;tea&#x27;: 12, &#x27;coffee&#x27;: 25, &#x27;juice&#x27;: 30}</pre>\n<p>Like a list, a dictionary passed to a function can be changed by the function.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the function <code>raise_price(menu, item, amount)</code>, which increases the price of <code>item</code> by <code>amount</code> if the item is on the menu, and otherwise adds it with the price <code>amount</code>. It changes <code>menu</code> and returns nothing.</p>\n<p>For example, after <code>m = {\"tea\": 10}</code> and <code>raise_price(m, \"tea\", 2)</code>, <code>m</code> is <code>{'tea': 12}</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "# Define raise_price(menu, item, amount): change menu itself.\n\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your code; comment it out before Check ----\n# m = {\"tea\": 10}\n# raise_price(m, \"tea\", 2)\n# print(m)\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "m = {\"tea\": 10}\nraise_price(m, \"tea\", 2)\nprint(m)",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "{'tea': 12}",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "m = {\"tea\": 10}\nraise_price(m, \"juice\", 30)\nprint(m)",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "{'tea': 10, 'juice': 30}",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "m = {}\nraise_price(m, \"a\", 1)\nraise_price(m, \"a\", 1)\nprint(m)",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "{'a': 2}",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "m = {\"x\": 5, \"y\": 7}\nr = raise_price(m, \"y\", -7)\nprint(m, r)",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "{'x': 5, 'y': 0} None",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    }
   ]
