  {
   "xml_index": 14,
   "xml_name": "L09_014_Looping Over Keys",
   "display_name": "Looping Over Keys",
   "questiontext_html": "<p><code>for k in d:</code> loops over the <b>keys</b> of a dictionary, in the order they were added. Inside the loop, <code>d[k]</code> gives each value.</p>\n<pre>marks = {&quot;Asha&quot;: 82, &quot;Ravi&quot;: 67, &quot;Meera&quot;: 91}\ntotal = 0\nfor name in marks:\n    total = total + marks[name]\nprint(total)</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>240</pre>\n<p><b>Indentation reminder:</b> the body of an <code>if</code>, loop, function or class must be indented (press Tab or type 4 spaces). Only the spaces at the start of a line matter.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the function <code>bill(order, menu)</code>. <code>order</code> is a dictionary from item names to quantities, and <code>menu</code> is a dictionary from item names to prices. Return the total cost of the order. Every ordered item is on the menu.</p>\n<p>For example, <code>bill({\"tea\": 2, \"samosa\": 3}, {\"tea\": 10, \"coffee\": 25, \"samosa\": 15})</code> returns <code>65</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "# Define bill(order, menu).\n\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your code; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(bill({\"tea\": 2, \"samosa\": 3}, {\"tea\": 10, \"coffee\": 25, \"samosa\": 15}))\n",
