  {
   "xml_index": 20,
   "xml_name": "L09_020_Dictionary From Two Lists",
   "display_name": "Dictionary From Two Lists",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Recall <code>zip(a, b)</code> from Lab 8: it pairs up two lists position by position. <code>dict(zip(keys, values))</code> turns two lists into a dictionary in one line:</p>\n<pre>names = [&quot;Asha&quot;, &quot;Ravi&quot;]\nmarks = [82, 67]\nprint(dict(zip(names, marks)))</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>{&#x27;Asha&#x27;: 82, &#x27;Ravi&#x27;: 67}</pre>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the function <code>make_dict(keys, values)</code>, which returns a dictionary pairing the items of the two lists <code>keys</code> and <code>values</code> (of the same length) position by position.</p>\n<p>For example, <code>make_dict([\"a\", \"b\"], [1, 2])</code> returns <code>{'a': 1, 'b': 2}</code>.</p>",
