  {
   "xml_index": 21,
   "xml_name": "L09_021_Invert A Dictionary",
   "display_name": "Invert A Dictionary",
   "questiontext_html": "<p><b>Inverting</b> a dictionary swaps its keys and values: <code>{\"Goa\": \"Panaji\"}</code> becomes <code>{\"Panaji\": \"Goa\"}</code>. This works when all the values are different (and immutable, since they become keys).</p>\n<p><b>Indentation reminder:</b> the body of an <code>if</code>, loop, function or class must be indented (press Tab or type 4 spaces). Only the spaces at the start of a line matter.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the function <code>invert(d)</code>, which returns a new dictionary where each value of <code>d</code> becomes a key and its key becomes the value. All values of <code>d</code> are different. Keep the order of <code>d</code>.</p>\n<p>For example, <code>invert({\"Goa\": \"Panaji\", \"Assam\": \"Dispur\"})</code> returns <code>{'Panaji': 'Goa', 'Dispur': 'Assam'}</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "# Define invert(d).\n\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your code; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(invert({\"Goa\": \"Panaji\", \"Assam\": \"Dispur\"}))\n",
