  {
   "xml_index": 22,
   "xml_name": "L09_022_Nested Dictionaries",
   "display_name": "Nested Dictionaries",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>A dictionary's values can be dictionaries. This is a natural way to store <b>records</b>: here each student's name maps to a dictionary of their marks.</p>\n<pre>students = {&quot;Asha&quot;: {&quot;maths&quot;: 90, &quot;physics&quot;: 78},\n            &quot;Ravi&quot;: {&quot;maths&quot;: 65, &quot;physics&quot;: 88}}</pre>\n<table style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:2px 1px;margin:6px 0 4px\"><tr><td rowspan=\"2\" style=\"padding-right:10px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace\">students =</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:4px 8px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:13px;background:#cfdcec;color:#1f3a63;border-radius:2px 2px 0 0\">&#x27;Asha&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:4px 8px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:13px;background:#cfdcec;color:#1f3a63;border-radius:2px 2px 0 0\">&#x27;Ravi&#x27;</td><td style=\"padding-left:8px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">key<br><br>value</td></tr><tr><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 8px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(31,95,153);color:#fff;border-radius:0 0 2px 2px\">{&#x27;maths&#x27;: 90, &#x27;physics&#x27;: 78}</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 8px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(74,163,223);color:#fff;border-radius:0 0 2px 2px\">{&#x27;maths&#x27;: 65, &#x27;physics&#x27;: 88}</td></tr></table>\n<table style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:2px 1px;margin:6px 0 4px\"><tr><td rowspan=\"2\" style=\"padding-right:10px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace\">students[&#x27;Asha&#x27;] =</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:4px 8px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:13px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px 2px 0 0\">&#x27;maths&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:4px 8px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:13px;background:#cfdcec;color:#1f3a63;border-radius:2px 2px 0 0\">&#x27;physics&#x27;</td><td style=\"padding-left:8px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">key<br><br>value</td></tr><tr><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 8px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:0 0 2px 2px\">90</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 8px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(74,163,223);color:#fff;border-radius:0 0 2px 2px\">78</td></tr></table><div style=\"font-size:13px;color:#8a939c;margin:0 0 10px\">students[&#x27;Asha&#x27;][&#x27;physics&#x27;] is 78</div>\n<p><b>Indentation reminder:</b> the body of an <code>if</code>, loop, function or class must be indented (press Tab or type 4 spaces). Only the spaces at the start of a line matter.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the function <code>subject_average(students, subject)</code>, where <code>students</code> is a non-empty dictionary like the one above and every student has marks for <code>subject</code>. Return the average mark in that subject, rounded to 2 decimal places with <code>round(value, 2)</code>.</p>\n<p>For example, <code>subject_average({\"Asha\": {\"maths\": 90}, \"Ravi\": {\"maths\": 65}}, \"maths\")</code> returns <code>77.5</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "# Define subject_average(students, subject).\n\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your code; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(subject_average({\"Asha\": {\"maths\": 90}, \"Ravi\": {\"maths\": 65}}, \"maths\"))\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "print(subject_average({\"Asha\": {\"maths\": 90}, \"Ravi\": {\"maths\": 65}}, \"maths\"))",
