  {
   "xml_index": 24,
   "xml_name": "L09_024_Removing Duplicates",
   "display_name": "Removing Duplicates",
   "questiontext_html": "<p><code>set</code> removes duplicates, and <code>sorted(s)</code> gives the items of a set as a sorted list. Together they give \"the different values, in order\":</p>\n<pre>print(sorted(set([5, 3, 5, 1, 3])))\nprint(sorted(set(&quot;banana&quot;)))</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>[1, 3, 5]\n[&#x27;a&#x27;, &#x27;b&#x27;, &#x27;n&#x27;]</pre>\n<p>The second line shows that <code>set(\"banana\")</code> is the set of different <b>letters</b>.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write two functions:</p>\n<ul><li><code>distinct_sorted(L)</code> returns a sorted list of the different values in the list <code>L</code>;</li><li><code>letters_used(word)</code> returns a sorted list of the different characters in the string <code>word</code>.</li></ul>\n<p>For example, <code>distinct_sorted([5, 3, 5, 1])</code> returns <code>[1, 3, 5]</code> and <code>letters_used(\"banana\")</code> returns <code>['a', 'b', 'n']</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "def distinct_sorted(L):\n    # write your code here\n\n\ndef letters_used(word):\n    # write your code here\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your code; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(distinct_sorted([5, 3, 5, 1]))\n# print(letters_used(\"banana\"))\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "print(distinct_sorted([5, 3, 5, 1]))",
     "stdin": "",
