  {
   "xml_index": 25,
   "xml_name": "L09_025_Adding To A Set",
   "display_name": "Adding To A Set",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Sets are mutable (items can be added and removed; the items themselves must be immutable, like dictionary keys):</p>\n<ul><li><code>s.add(x)</code> adds one item;</li><li><code>s.update(other)</code> adds every item of <code>other</code> (a list, a set, ...).</li></ul>\n<p>Adding something that is already there changes nothing.</p>\n<pre>s = {1, 2}\ns.add(3)\ns.add(2)\ns.update([4, 5, 1])\nprint(sorted(s))</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>[1, 2, 3, 4, 5]</pre>\n<p><b>Indentation reminder:</b> the body of an <code>if</code>, loop, function or class must be indented (press Tab or type 4 spaces). Only the spaces at the start of a line matter.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the function <code>all_tags(posts)</code>, where <code>posts</code> is a list of posts and each post is a list of tags (strings). Return a sorted list of all the different tags used in any post.</p>\n<p>For example, <code>all_tags([[\"python\", \"lists\"], [\"python\", \"sets\"]])</code> returns <code>['lists', 'python', 'sets']</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "# Define all_tags(posts): collect the tags in a set.\n\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your code; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(all_tags([[\"python\", \"lists\"], [\"python\", \"sets\"]]))\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "print(all_tags([[\"python\", \"lists\"], [\"python\", \"sets\"]]))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "['lists', 'python', 'sets']",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(all_tags([]))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "[]",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(all_tags([[], ['a']]))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "['a']",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(all_tags([[\"x\", \"x\"], [\"y\"], [\"x\", \"z\"]]))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "['x', 'y', 'z']",
     "extra": "",
