  {
   "xml_index": 28,
   "xml_name": "L09_028_Union",
   "display_name": "Union",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Sets support the operations from mathematics. The <b>union</b> <code>a | b</code> (or <code>a.union(b)</code>) contains everything that is in <code>a</code>, in <code>b</code>, or in both:</p>\n<div style=\"position:relative;width:310px;height:175px;margin:6px 0 4px\"><div style=\"position:absolute;left:10px;top:18px;width:170px;height:150px;border-radius:50%;border:2px solid #2b4c7e;background:rgba(43,76,126,.07)\"></div><div style=\"position:absolute;left:120px;top:18px;width:170px;height:150px;border-radius:50%;border:2px solid #2a8c8c;background:rgba(42,140,140,.07)\"></div><div style=\"position:absolute;left:60px;top:0;font-weight:600;color:#2b4c7e\">a</div><div style=\"position:absolute;left:230px;top:0;font-weight:600;color:#2a8c8c\">b</div><div style=\"position:absolute;left:28px;top:55px;width:66px;text-align:center\"><div style=\"background:#2b4c7e;color:#fff;border-radius:3px;padding:1px 5px;margin:2px 0;font-family:monospace;font-size:13px;white-space:nowrap;display:inline-block\">1</div><br><div style=\"background:#2b4c7e;color:#fff;border-radius:3px;padding:1px 5px;margin:2px 0;font-family:monospace;font-size:13px;white-space:nowrap;display:inline-block\">2</div><br></div><div style=\"position:absolute;left:128px;top:55px;width:66px;text-align:center\"><div style=\"background:#2b4c7e;color:#fff;border-radius:3px;padding:1px 5px;margin:2px 0;font-family:monospace;font-size:13px;white-space:nowrap;display:inline-block\">3</div><br><div style=\"background:#2b4c7e;color:#fff;border-radius:3px;padding:1px 5px;margin:2px 0;font-family:monospace;font-size:13px;white-space:nowrap;display:inline-block\">4</div><br></div><div style=\"position:absolute;left:214px;top:55px;width:66px;text-align:center\"><div style=\"background:#2b4c7e;color:#fff;border-radius:3px;padding:1px 5px;margin:2px 0;font-family:monospace;font-size:13px;white-space:nowrap;display:inline-block\">5</div><br><div style=\"background:#2b4c7e;color:#fff;border-radius:3px;padding:1px 5px;margin:2px 0;font-family:monospace;font-size:13px;white-space:nowrap;display:inline-block\">6</div><br></div></div><div style=\"font-size:13px;color:#8a939c;margin:0 0 10px\">a | b is {1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6}</div>\n<pre>a = {1, 2, 3, 4}\nb = {3, 4, 5, 6}\nprint(sorted(a | b))</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>[1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]</pre>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the function <code>all_members(club1, club2)</code>, where the two lists contain the names of the members of two clubs. Return a sorted list of everyone who is in at least one club (each name once).</p>\n<p>For example, <code>all_members([\"Asha\", \"Ravi\"], [\"Ravi\", \"Meera\"])</code> returns <code>['Asha', 'Meera', 'Ravi']</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "# Define all_members(club1, club2): use a union.\n\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your code; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(all_members([\"Asha\", \"Ravi\"], [\"Ravi\", \"Meera\"]))\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "print(all_members([\"Asha\", \"Ravi\"], [\"Ravi\", \"Meera\"]))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "['Asha', 'Meera', 'Ravi']",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(all_members([], []))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "[]",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(all_members([\"a\", \"a\"], [\"b\"]))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "['a', 'b']",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(all_members([\"x\", \"y\"], [\"y\", \"x\"]))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "['x', 'y']",
     "extra": "",
