  {
   "xml_index": 29,
   "xml_name": "L09_029_Intersection",
   "display_name": "Intersection",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>The <b>intersection</b> <code>a &amp; b</code> (or <code>a.intersection(b)</code>) contains only the items that are in <b>both</b> sets:</p>\n<div style=\"position:relative;width:310px;height:175px;margin:6px 0 4px\"><div style=\"position:absolute;left:10px;top:18px;width:170px;height:150px;border-radius:50%;border:2px solid #2b4c7e;background:rgba(43,76,126,.07)\"></div><div style=\"position:absolute;left:120px;top:18px;width:170px;height:150px;border-radius:50%;border:2px solid #2a8c8c;background:rgba(42,140,140,.07)\"></div><div style=\"position:absolute;left:60px;top:0;font-weight:600;color:#2b4c7e\">a</div><div style=\"position:absolute;left:230px;top:0;font-weight:600;color:#2a8c8c\">b</div><div style=\"position:absolute;left:28px;top:55px;width:66px;text-align:center\"><div style=\"color:#8a939c;border-radius:3px;padding:1px 5px;margin:2px 0;font-family:monospace;font-size:13px;white-space:nowrap;display:inline-block\">1</div><br><div style=\"color:#8a939c;border-radius:3px;padding:1px 5px;margin:2px 0;font-family:monospace;font-size:13px;white-space:nowrap;display:inline-block\">2</div><br></div><div style=\"position:absolute;left:128px;top:55px;width:66px;text-align:center\"><div style=\"background:#2b4c7e;color:#fff;border-radius:3px;padding:1px 5px;margin:2px 0;font-family:monospace;font-size:13px;white-space:nowrap;display:inline-block\">3</div><br><div style=\"background:#2b4c7e;color:#fff;border-radius:3px;padding:1px 5px;margin:2px 0;font-family:monospace;font-size:13px;white-space:nowrap;display:inline-block\">4</div><br></div><div style=\"position:absolute;left:214px;top:55px;width:66px;text-align:center\"><div style=\"color:#8a939c;border-radius:3px;padding:1px 5px;margin:2px 0;font-family:monospace;font-size:13px;white-space:nowrap;display:inline-block\">5</div><br><div style=\"color:#8a939c;border-radius:3px;padding:1px 5px;margin:2px 0;font-family:monospace;font-size:13px;white-space:nowrap;display:inline-block\">6</div><br></div></div><div style=\"font-size:13px;color:#8a939c;margin:0 0 10px\">a &amp; b is {3, 4}</div>\n<pre>a = {1, 2, 3, 4}\nb = {3, 4, 5, 6}\nprint(sorted(a &amp; b))</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>[3, 4]</pre>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the function <code>common_friends(f1, f2)</code>, where the two lists are the friends of two people. Return a sorted list of the friends they have in common.</p>\n<p>For example, <code>common_friends([\"Asha\", \"Ravi\", \"Zoya\"], [\"Ravi\", \"Meera\", \"Zoya\"])</code> returns <code>['Ravi', 'Zoya']</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "# Define common_friends(f1, f2): use an intersection.\n\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your code; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(common_friends([\"Asha\", \"Ravi\", \"Zoya\"], [\"Ravi\", \"Meera\", \"Zoya\"]))\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "print(common_friends([\"Asha\", \"Ravi\", \"Zoya\"], [\"Ravi\", \"Meera\", \"Zoya\"]))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "['Ravi', 'Zoya']",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(common_friends([\"a\"], [\"b\"]))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "[]",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(common_friends([\"p\", \"q\", \"q\"], [\"q\", \"q\", \"p\"]))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "['p', 'q']",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
