  {
   "xml_index": 31,
   "xml_name": "L09_031_Symmetric Difference",
   "display_name": "Symmetric Difference",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>The <b>symmetric difference</b> <code>a ^ b</code> contains the items that are in <b>exactly one</b> of the two sets (in either, but not in both):</p>\n<div style=\"position:relative;width:310px;height:175px;margin:6px 0 4px\"><div style=\"position:absolute;left:10px;top:18px;width:170px;height:150px;border-radius:50%;border:2px solid #2b4c7e;background:rgba(43,76,126,.07)\"></div><div style=\"position:absolute;left:120px;top:18px;width:170px;height:150px;border-radius:50%;border:2px solid #2a8c8c;background:rgba(42,140,140,.07)\"></div><div style=\"position:absolute;left:60px;top:0;font-weight:600;color:#2b4c7e\">a</div><div style=\"position:absolute;left:230px;top:0;font-weight:600;color:#2a8c8c\">b</div><div style=\"position:absolute;left:28px;top:55px;width:66px;text-align:center\"><div style=\"background:#2b4c7e;color:#fff;border-radius:3px;padding:1px 5px;margin:2px 0;font-family:monospace;font-size:13px;white-space:nowrap;display:inline-block\">1</div><br><div style=\"background:#2b4c7e;color:#fff;border-radius:3px;padding:1px 5px;margin:2px 0;font-family:monospace;font-size:13px;white-space:nowrap;display:inline-block\">2</div><br></div><div style=\"position:absolute;left:128px;top:55px;width:66px;text-align:center\"><div style=\"color:#8a939c;border-radius:3px;padding:1px 5px;margin:2px 0;font-family:monospace;font-size:13px;white-space:nowrap;display:inline-block\">3</div><br><div style=\"color:#8a939c;border-radius:3px;padding:1px 5px;margin:2px 0;font-family:monospace;font-size:13px;white-space:nowrap;display:inline-block\">4</div><br></div><div style=\"position:absolute;left:214px;top:55px;width:66px;text-align:center\"><div style=\"background:#2b4c7e;color:#fff;border-radius:3px;padding:1px 5px;margin:2px 0;font-family:monospace;font-size:13px;white-space:nowrap;display:inline-block\">5</div><br><div style=\"background:#2b4c7e;color:#fff;border-radius:3px;padding:1px 5px;margin:2px 0;font-family:monospace;font-size:13px;white-space:nowrap;display:inline-block\">6</div><br></div></div><div style=\"font-size:13px;color:#8a939c;margin:0 0 10px\">a ^ b is {1, 2, 5, 6}</div>\n<p>It is the same as <code>(a | b) - (a &amp; b)</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the function <code>changed_answers(before, after)</code>, where the two lists contain the numbers of the questions a student marked for review before and after revising. Return a sorted list of the questions that are marked in exactly one of the two lists.</p>\n<p>For example, <code>changed_answers([1, 2, 3], [2, 3, 4])</code> returns <code>[1, 4]</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "# Define changed_answers(before, after): use a symmetric difference.\n\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your code; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(changed_answers([1, 2, 3], [2, 3, 4]))\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "print(changed_answers([1, 2, 3], [2, 3, 4]))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "[1, 4]",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(changed_answers([1], [1]))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "[]",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(changed_answers([], [5, 6]))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "[5, 6]",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(changed_answers([9, 8, 7], [1]))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "[1, 7, 8, 9]",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    }
   ]
