  {
   "xml_index": 32,
   "xml_name": "L09_032_Subsets",
   "display_name": "Subsets",
   "questiontext_html": "<p><code>a &lt;= b</code> (or <code>a.issubset(b)</code>) is <code>True</code> when <b>every</b> item of <code>a</code> is also in <code>b</code>: <code>a</code> is a <b>subset</b> of <code>b</code>. Likewise <code>a &gt;= b</code> asks whether <code>a</code> contains all of <code>b</code> (a <b>superset</b>).</p>\n<pre>print({1, 2} &lt;= {1, 2, 3})\nprint({1, 4} &lt;= {1, 2, 3})\nprint(set() &lt;= {1})</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>True\nFalse\nTrue</pre>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the function <code>can_spell(word, tiles)</code>, which returns <code>True</code> if every letter used in <code>word</code> appears at least once in the string <code>tiles</code> (how many times does not matter here), and <code>False</code> otherwise.</p>\n<p>For example, <code>can_spell(\"cab\", \"abcde\")</code> returns <code>True</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "# Define can_spell(word, tiles): use a subset test.\n\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your code; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(can_spell(\"cab\", \"abcde\"))\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "print(can_spell(\"cab\", \"abcde\"))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "True",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(can_spell(\"dog\", \"gdx\"))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "False",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(can_spell(\"\", \"a\"))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "True",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(can_spell(\"aaa\", \"a\"))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "True",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
