  {
   "xml_index": 33,
   "xml_name": "L09_033_Frozen Sets",
   "display_name": "Frozen Sets",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>A normal set is mutable, so (like a list) it cannot be a dictionary key or an item of another set. <code>frozenset(...)</code> makes an <b>immutable</b> set: it has no <code>add</code> or <code>remove</code>, but it <b>can</b> be put inside a set or used as a key. Two frozensets with the same items are equal, whatever order the items were given in.</p>\n<pre>t1 = frozenset([&quot;Asha&quot;, &quot;Ravi&quot;])\nt2 = frozenset([&quot;Ravi&quot;, &quot;Asha&quot;])\nprint(t1 == t2)\nteams = set()\nteams.add(t1)\nteams.add(t2)\nprint(len(teams))</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>True\n1</pre>\n<p><b>Indentation reminder:</b> the body of an <code>if</code>, loop, function or class must be indented (press Tab or type 4 spaces). Only the spaces at the start of a line matter.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the function <code>distinct_teams(teams)</code>, where <code>teams</code> is a list of teams and each team is a list of names. Two teams are the same if they have the same members, in any order. Return how many different teams there are.</p>\n<p>For example, <code>distinct_teams([[\"a\", \"b\"], [\"b\", \"a\"], [\"a\", \"c\"]])</code> returns <code>2</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "# Define distinct_teams(teams): put frozensets into a set.\n\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your code; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(distinct_teams([[\"a\", \"b\"], [\"b\", \"a\"], [\"a\", \"c\"]]))\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "print(distinct_teams([[\"a\", \"b\"], [\"b\", \"a\"], [\"a\", \"c\"]]))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "2",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(distinct_teams([]))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "0",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(distinct_teams([[\"x\"], [\"x\"], [\"x\"]]))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "1",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(distinct_teams([[\"p\", \"q\", \"r\"], [\"r\", \"q\", \"p\"], [\"p\", \"q\"]]))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "2",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    }
   ]
  },
