   "xml_index": 35,
   "xml_name": "L09_035_Anagrams",
   "display_name": "Anagrams",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Now choose the right tools yourself: a dictionary to look things up or count, a set to remove duplicates or compare groups, a list to keep order. Test with small examples, including empty inputs.</p>\n<p>Two words are <b>anagrams</b> if they use exactly the same letters, <b>the same number of times</b> each (for example \"listen\" and \"silent\"). Comparing sets is not enough here (\"aab\" and \"abb\" have the same set of letters); compare letter <b>counts</b> instead. Two dictionaries are equal (<code>==</code>) when they have the same pairs, whatever their order.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the function <code>is_anagram(w1, w2)</code>, which returns <code>True</code> if the lowercase words <code>w1</code> and <code>w2</code> are anagrams, and <code>False</code> otherwise.</p>\n<p>For example, <code>is_anagram(\"listen\", \"silent\")</code> returns <code>True</code> and <code>is_anagram(\"aab\", \"abb\")</code> returns <code>False</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "# Define is_anagram(w1, w2).\n\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your code; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(is_anagram(\"listen\", \"silent\"))\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
